<title>NEW ZEALAND: RUGBY UNION-AUCKLAND BEAT QUEENSLAND 49-26.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-AUCKLAND BEAT QUEENSLAND 49-26.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND, New Zealand 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Auckland Blues beat the Queensland Reds 49-26 (halftime 17-6) in their super 12 rugby union match at Eden Park on Monday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Auckland - Tries: Brian Lima (2), Andrew Blowers (2), Joeli Vidiri, Carlos Spencer tries. Conversions: Adrian Cashmore (5). Penalty goals: Cashmore (3).</p>
<p>Queensland - Tries: Jason Little, Matthew Pini. Penalty goals: John Eales (4). Conversions: Eales (2).</p>
</text>
